<h3>Open Trailers vs. Enclosed Containerized Carriers: A Comparative Analysis</h3>

While enclosed carriers provide the highest level of protection, open trailers are the more common and economical choice for car transportation. Open trailers typically have an open-air platform for vehicles, which has the following benefits and drawbacks:

